[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human neurons (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=9,146): skew = 0.048, excess kurtosis = 0.133, D'Agostino K^2 p = 0.00822, Jarque-Bera p = 0.0061
  Normality of residuals: skew = 0.004, excess kurtosis = 0.439, D'Agostino K^2 p = 9.72e-12, Jarque-Bera p = 1.08e-16
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 181.193, p = 7.48e-14
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 0.741, p = 0.477
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/ribonn/neurons/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_ribonn_neurons.png
